Disgrace news
=============

0.1.2
-----
- Fix off-by-one orphan instrument: new projects start with the default
  track using the default instrument, and XRNS import drops unreferenced
  shared instruments, so repeated track joins no longer leave the
  instrument list one entry longer than necessary.
- Audio engine: lock-free thread-pool fan-out without per-block
  allocations, non-blocking DSSI sandbox handoff, allocation-free
  SFZ/XRNI voice recycling, TTS synthesis kept off the realtime thread,
  cheaper per-sample DSP (cached ADSR/envelope steps, hoisted filter and
  compressor constants, fused copy/gain passes).
- GUI stays responsive on large songs: mixer meters throttled and gated to
  the visible tab, transport bar avoids redundant relayouts, order-list
  copies removed from per-frame drawing, list rebuilds use Freeze/Thaw.

0.1.1
-----
- Deleting a track (including the tracker Join to Previous/Next) now also
  removes its instrument when no other track uses it.
- Joining hands the source instrument over to the target track when the
  target has none, so joined notes stay audible.

0.1.0
-----
Initial public release.
